course: dictionary
lesson: 8174
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on the subject you are learning. The word resistance is one of them. Context, the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning is right. «Air resistance slows a parachute.» In a science lesson, this means a force that slows down a moving thing.
explain: The same word can also describe a body or a germ. «Every time antibiotics are used, the few bacteria that happen to survive can multiply.» Here resistance is about a germ surviving a medicine. Ask yourself: what is the topic? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Antibiotic resistance means the bacteria change so the medicine stops working; it is the bacteria that become resistant, not the person's body.» The sentence tells you exactly who or what is resistant, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Resistance can mean fighting against something or refusing to accept it.
fact: In science, resistance is a force that slows down a moving thing, like air resistance or water resistance.
fact: In electricity, resistance is how much a material makes it hard for current to flow.
fact: «Antibiotic resistance» means the bacteria change so that a medicine stops working.
fact: «The path of least resistance» means the easiest way.
exercise: «Air resistance slows a parachute.» What does resistance mean here? | *A force that slows down a moving thing | A wire that carries current | Fighting against the parachute | The ability of the body to fight illness
exercise: «Antibiotic resistance means the bacteria change so the medicine stops working.» Which one is resistant? | *The bacteria | The person's body | The doctor | The medicine
exercise: What does «the path of least resistance» mean? | The hardest way to go | A road with no trees | A way with lots of water | *The easiest way
test: In electricity, what does resistance describe? | *How much a material makes it hard for current to flow | How heavy a wire is | How fast a current flows | The colour of a wire
test: What is the body's resistance to illness? | The way a germ spreads | The speed of a heartbeat | *The ability to fight off illness | A type of medicine
exam: Mia says resistance always means fighting a war. Is she right? | Yes, resistance always means fighting in a war | *No, resistance has several meanings, and fighting is only one of them | No, resistance is a type of food | Yes, but only in science lessons
